# Pin the line endings of every signed text file, so that a fresh checkout on any platform
# (core.autocrlf=true or false) produces the same bytes.  verify_local_prune_rtl.py additionally
# hashes the canonical LF form, so the signature is verifiable even in a foreign working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Formal VCD witnesses are frozen evidence: git must never rewrite their bytes
# (no EOL normalisation).  The NP4B binding additionally folds CRLF/CR to LF, so
# even a historically rewritten tree verifies identically.
*.vcd -text -eol
*.wdb binary
*.dcp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary
*.xcf binary
